config FREETZ_PACKAGE_FREETZ_MATTER
	bool "freetz-matter 0.1 (FRITZ!Box as a Matter device)"
	depends on FREETZ_TARGET_UCLIBC_1_0_58_MIN
	depends on FREETZ_TARGET_IPV6_SUPPORT
	default n
	select FREETZ_PACKAGE_ALSA_UTILS
	help
		Exposes the FRITZ!Box itself as a Matter device, so a Matter
		controller (Apple Home, Google Home, Alexa, Home Assistant,
		python-matter-server, ...) can commission and read or control the
		box without any hub software and without Node.js.

		Built on project-chip/rs-matter, the pure-Rust Matter stack.

		Endpoints:
		 - Temperature Sensor (0x0302 / cluster 0x0402): the same
		   sensor chain the box_info page uses
		   (/proc/chip_temperature, the thermal zone, the AVM
		   power-management temperature and /proc/avm/temp_sensors).
		 - Smart Speaker (0x0022, OnOff + LevelControl): mute/unmute and
		   volume of the ALSA playback path (amixer, from alsa-utils).
		 - Root node BasicInformation carries the real vendor, model,
		   firmware version and serial number of the box.

		The application is built with Rust/Cargo and installs
		/usr/bin/freetz-matter, the rc.freetz-matter init script and the
		Freetz configuration (port, fabric store location, verbosity).

		After the first start the commissioning QR code and manual pairing
		code are written to the service log
		(http://fritz.box:81/cgi-bin/status/mod/logs -> rc.freetz-matter),
		because the device starts uncommissioned.

		No other Freetz-EVO package is required, in either direction.
		Optional companions: openthread/ot-br-posix if the box should also
		serve as a Thread border router, and any Matter controller (Home
		Assistant, or python-matter-server on a glibc host) to commission
		this device.

		matter-bridge is optional: its native controller can commission
		this device automatically for the local Domoticz Matter driver.
		Run matter-bridge-setup for that local chain.
		The two packages coexist without conflicts:
		matter-bridge serves WebSocket on TCP 5580, this device is a Matter
		node on UDP 5540.

		Can be externalized (External menu): /usr/bin/freetz-matter is the
		whole payload (4.5 MB) and is moved to external storage; the init
		script, the configuration and the fabric store stay in the firmware.
